# Every text file checks out with LF, on Windows too (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true).
# World Packs are YAML: a CRLF inside a block scalar would change a string, then a fact, then AC-8's
# Windows record (docs/DECISIONS.md ARC-49; step-14 §13.10.1 W-3).
* text=auto eol=lf
# The one file committed with CRLF keeps its bytes: it is a third party's licence text, never renormalized.
clients/3d-spike/assets/characters/LICENSE.quaternius-ual.txt -text

# glTF binary buffers and GLB containers are binary data. Git's own test (a NUL byte in
# the first 8000 bytes) misses some of them: bar_chair_round_01.bin was diffed as text,
# and a diff with invalid UTF-8 broke the acceptance scan that reads `git diff` output
# (tests/acceptance/tests/precursor_vocabulary.rs).
*.bin binary
*.glb binary
*.sqlite binary
# A World Pack's data files are the same bytes on every platform (Windows' autocrlf included), so the
# NOTICE's byte and line counts hold everywhere; the weather pack still reads CRLF (DECISIONS.md DEP-31).
worlds/*/data/**/*.csv text eol=lf
# Recorded model outputs (cassettes, ARC-58) are JSON Lines whose entries are hashed: a Windows
# checkout must keep them LF, as they were written (pr-s10-p5-backends.md D-P5-13).
*.jsonl text eol=lf
# The generated decision index holds one row per record (docs/DECISIONS.md §3): a local merge keeps
# both sides' new rows, and scripts/check_decision_ids.py reports the index stale if their order is off.
docs/decisions/INDEX.md merge=union

# S26-c (operator ruling 2026-10-19): the cast's generated characters are stored with Git LFS, so the
# repository's history does not grow by ~10 MB per Person. Only the buffers and textures: the .gltf
# (JSON, ~22 kB) and the .import files stay plain text. A checkout without LFS gets pointer files; the
# 3D client then draws that Person as the town figure (cast_binding.gd), so CI does not need LFS.
clients/3d-spike/assets/characters/cast/**/*.bin filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
clients/3d-spike/assets/characters/cast/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
